creatures.courtyard.apparition.descripti:
{green|Ephemeral Apparition}

There is a phenomenon, when you take a picture of recently deceased you can sometimes spot something unusual. A flicker of light hovering in place where the person has passed. Clearly not an undead manifestation, this is something else entirely. Just remaining there for a time, floating gently yet spreading a bone-chilling aura, and almost impossible to dissipate prematurely with physical contact.

{gold|Special Ability : Teleporting. No morale. Mind immunity. Undead. Non-living. Immune to Earth and Animate Dead spells. Ephemeral}
Apparitions are more ghostish even than Ghosts. They disappear at the beginning of the second subsequent round (third with Migdigravia). They can teleport at speed 5, but perform no attacks or retaliations. But they are almost immune for physical and magical attacks (98% reduction). Their presence gives living enemy stacks a 10% chance of losing their turn to Fear, subject to fear immunity. Several Apparition stacks do not multiply this chance. There is only one situation to see Apparitions - they can be summoned by Camera Obscura war machine.

{gold|Stack Experience:} Immune to Armageddon from rank 3, if the stack has the required experience.

creatures.courtyard.arquebusier.descript:
{green|Arquebusier}

Arquebusiers and Musketeers, armed with dangerous novelty weapons, are feared by their enemies during battles. While the muskets fueled with explosive powder are normally subject to range penalties, their projectiles are devastating even to well armored targets.

{gold|Special Ability: Shooter. Ignore Defense 15%}
Attacks ignore 15% of enemy Defense.

{gold|Stack Experience:}
Double damage chance increases by 5 percentage points per rank (50% at rank 10). Ignore Defense reaches 20/25/30/35/40% at ranks 3/5/7/9/10. From rank 6 can shoot while blocked; from rank 9 suffers no distance penalty.

The ranked defense penetration values are totals and do not stack with the innate bonus.

creatures.courtyard.battleDodo.descripti:
{green|Battle Dodo}

The exotic Dodo birds that were discovered recently are a weird folk. They feared no death nor adversity and fight with even greated dedication when the opponent is imposing. Some of these huge birds embrace imported culture and don iron armors to become immovable bulwarks inspired by the tales of knights slaying great beasts, while others stick to their traditions and fight with such ferocity, that they mortify their non-dodo allies.

{gold|Special Ability : Fearless. Affected by permanent Slayer spell. Spell Resistance Aura. General Damage Reduction 25%. Spell Damage Reduction 33%. Defensive stance}
Dodos are immune to Fear and enchanted with permanent Expert Slayer. They reduce physical damage from melee and ranged attacks by 25%. Battle Dodos have 20% innate Magic Resistance and grant adjacent allied units a 20% Magic Resistance Aura. Both increase with stack experience. They reduce spell damage by 33% and gain +5 Defense while defending.

{gold|Stack Experience:}
Innate Magic Resistance and resistance aura reach 25/30/35/40% at ranks 4/6/8/9. Additional melee damage reduction reaches 5/10/15/20/25% at ranks 3/5/7/9/10, applied separately from the innate 25% physical damage reduction (43.75% combined at rank 10, before other modifiers).

Under Auk, the aura is doubled (40–80%), innate Magic Resistance is at least 33%, and spell damage reduction rises to 45%.

creatures.courtyard.cupid.description:
{green|Cupid}

Cupids are magically animated sculptures, much like Gargoyles and Golems. While the aristocracy indeed fancies them as guards of their estates, many Cupids are comissioned just to show off owner's wealth or serve as companions.

{gold|Special Ability : Flying. Gargoyle. Mind Immunity.}

{gold|Stack Experience:} Magic resistance increases by 3 percentage points per rank (up to 30%). Returns to its original hex after striking from rank 5 and prevents enemy retaliation from rank 8.

creatures.courtyard.dodo.description:
{green|Dodo}

The exotic Dodo birds that were discovered recently are a weird folk. They feared no death nor adversity and fight with even greated dedication when the opponent is imposing. Some of these huge birds embrace imported culture and don iron armors to become immovable bulwarks inspired by the tales of knights slaying great beasts, while others stick to their traditions and fight with such ferocity, that they mortify their non-dodo allies.

{gold|Special Ability : Fearless. Affected by permanent Slayer spell}
Dodos are immune to Fear and enchanted with permanent Advanced Slayer.

{gold|Stack Experience:}
Magic Mirror increases by 5 percentage points per rank (50% at rank 10). Advanced Slayer becomes Expert at rank 5. One additional retaliation from rank 5, two from rank 9. From rank 8, strikes first when retaliating against melee attacks, if retaliation is possible.

The rank-based Slayer mastery replaces the innate mastery rather than adding a second spell effect.

creatures.courtyard.fireNewt.description:
{green|Salamander}

Salamander is a name applied to a wide range of non-elemental creatures originating from the Elemental Plane of Fire. Due to their elemental affinity they cannot be affected by fire spells. Thanks to that, many alchemists employ them to tend to furnaces or other works involving sustained exposition to fire or heat.

{gold|Special Ability : Immune to Fire}
Although Salamanders are immune to fire magic, they are not unaffected by fire-based creature attacks. For example Magogs' fireball attack or Dragons' breath attacks are not considered to be magical and therefore they do harm Salamanders.

{gold|Stack Experience:}
Fire Shield reflects 5 percentage points more damage per rank, up to 50%. From rank 4, positive spells can bypass natural spell immunity (Receptive).

Innate and cast Fire Shield do not stack; the stronger effect applies. Nefefareen grants Receptive to both Salamanders and, while under an actual Fire Shield spell, +2 Speed, +2 minimum and maximum damage, at least 1 Morale and a 33% chance of Immolation after attacking.

creatures.courtyard.gildedHomunculus.des:
{green|Gilded Homunculus}

Homunculi are more like animals than people. They are produced in a complex alchemical reaction and are small, disproportionate, yet strong caricatures of the proper human beings. They are usually tasked with works that need considerable strength, human-level agility and intelligence of a dog. Valuable asset on the battlefield since they not only regenerate wounds at impressive rate, the presence of Gilded Homunculi slightly amplifies power of damaging spells.

{gold|Special Ability : Regeneration. Damage spells power increasing}
Homunculus Regeneration enables the top creature of the stack to regain 10 health each combat round. Additionally, the presence in the hero's army increases the hero's spell damage by 15% for all magic schools (not Spell Power). Splitting the stack does not multiply this bonus.

{gold|Stack Experience:}
Regeneration reaches 11/12/13/14/15 HP at ranks 2/4/6/8/10. Defensive Stance from rank 5 (+5 Defense when defending); melee damage reduction reaches 5/10/15/20% at ranks 3/5/7/9. Hero spell damage bonus remains 15%.

creatures.courtyard.graniteCupid.descrip:
{green|Granite Cupid}

Cupids are magically animated sculptures, much like Gargoyles and Golems. While the aristocracy indeed fancies them as guards of their estates, many Cupids are comissioned just to show off owner's wealth or serve as companions. Despite their graceful movements, Granite Cupids' strikes are heavy enough to render their targets unconscious.

{gold|Special Ability : Flying. Gargoyle. Mind Immunity. 20% chance to cast Stun after attack}
Stunned creatures cannot act or retaliate for up to two turns; being attacked ends the stun. Undead, Gargoyle, Non-living and immune to mind creatures are immune to Stun attack.

{gold|Stack Experience:}
Stun chance reaches 25/30/35/40% at ranks 3/5/7/9 (total chance, not added to the base 20%). Magic resistance reaches 5/10/15% at ranks 5/7/9.

creatures.courtyard.greaterDodo.descript:
{green|Grand Dodo}

The exotic Dodo birds that were discovered recently are a weird folk. They feared no death nor adversity and fight with even greated dedication when the opponent is imposing. Some of these huge birds embrace imported culture and don iron armors to become immovable bulwarks inspired by the tales of knights slaying great beasts, while others stick to their traditions and fight with such ferocity, that they mortify their non-dodo allies.

{gold|Special Ability : Fearless. Affected by permanent Slayer spell. Triple strike}
Dodos are immune to Fear and enchanted with Expert Slayer. They can attack three times per attack but they never retaliate to enemy attacks (this does not prevent enemies from retaliating). Grand Dodos reduce the morale of allied non-Dodo creatures by 1.

{gold|Stack Experience:}
Ranged damage reduction reaches 10/15/20/25/30/35% at ranks 2/4/6/7/9/10. Attacks ignore 5/10/15/20% of enemy Defense at ranks 4/6/8/10. No resistance aura.

creatures.courtyard.homunculus.descripti:
{green|Homunculus}

Homunculi are more like animals than people. They are produced in a complex alchemical reaction and are small, disproportionate, yet strong caricatures of the proper human beings. They are usually tasked with works that need considerable strength, human-level agility and intelligence of a dog. Valuable asset on the battlefield since they regenerate wounds at impressive rate.

{gold|Special Ability : Regeneration}
Homunculus Regeneration enables the top creature of the stack to regain 7 health each combat round.

{gold|Stack Experience:}
Regeneration restores 8–15 HP at ranks 1–8 and fully heals the wounded creature from rank 9; it never resurrects fallen creatures. Jousting from rank 4 (+5% damage per hex travelled); Defensive Stance from rank 6 (+5 Defense when defending). Chance to cast Disrupting Ray before an attack increases by 5 percentage points per rank, up to 50%.

creatures.courtyard.jabberwock.descripti:
{green|Jabberwock}

Jabberwocks, despite their appearances, are not related to dragons. Those foul creatures dwell in corrupted caverns and terrorize every living being within their reach. Scarlet ones, with scales tinted by bloodshed, can decimate a numerous army in a single sweep of their claws. It is no surprise that the mere sight of these monsters can paralyze with fear.

{gold|Special Ability : Flying}
Jabberwocks are susceptible to Advanced and Expert Slayer (KING2).

{gold|Stack Experience:}
Physical damage reduction reaches 5/10/15/20/25/30/35% at ranks 2/4/6/7/8/9/10. Magic Resistance reaches 10/15/20/25/30/35% at ranks 3/5/7/8/9/10. Unlimited retaliations from rank 5. From rank 7, retaliates before enemy melee attacks when retaliation is possible. Regenerates up to 40/60/80 HP of the wounded creature each round at ranks 8/9/10 (does not resurrect).

creatures.courtyard.mandrake.description:
{green|Mandrake}

Mandrakes are violent and whimsical creatures, while at the same time highly cultured. Their singing voices can cause an agonizing death and to make things worse for their victims, they spread the vines around the battlefield to entangle anyone who dares approach them.

{gold|Special Ability : Summon Guardians}
At the beginning of each battle, Mandrakes summon guardians — Tangle Vines. Vines occupy accessible hexes surrounding the stack. Each summoned stack contains twice as many Vines as the summoning stack contains Mandrakes. But beware! At the beginning, the Tangle Vines block the Mandrakes, preventing them from moving. Mandrakes should be positioned wisely within the army (not in the corners) to keep as many free hexes as possible for vine summoning.

{gold|Stack Experience:}
Enemy hero spells cost 1/2/3/4/5 extra mana from ranks 2/4/6/8/10 (only the strongest stack applies). From ranks 4/6/8/10, has a 20/30/40/50% chance to cast Basic Weakness after a melee attack. Blocks retaliation from rank 5, binds enemies after melee attacks from rank 7, and fully regenerates the surviving top creature at the start of its turn from rank 10.

Ophrys grants both Mandrakes +5 HP and both vine types +1 Speed and melee First Strike.

{green|Monstrous Jabberwock}

Jabberwocks, despite their appearances, are not related to dragons. Those foul creatures dwell in corrupted caverns and terrorize every living being within their reach. Scarlet ones, with scales tinted by bloodshed, can decimate a numerous army in a single sweep of their claws. It is no surprise that the mere sight of these monsters can paralyze with fear.

{gold|Special Ability : Flying. Fear. Destruction}
Monstrous Jabberwocks are susceptible to Advanced and Expert Slayer (KING2). Living enemy stacks have a 10% chance of losing their turn to Fear (subject to fear immunity); splitting Monstrous Jabberwocks into several stacks does not multiply this chance. Decimation has a 25% chance after an attack to kill 10% of the remaining creatures in the target stack, rounded down.

{gold|Stack Experience:}
Mind immunity from rank 3. Acid damage after attacks: 5/10/15/20/25% chance at ranks 1/4/6/8/10; deals 5/10/15/20/25/30 damage per creature at ranks 1/4/6/8/9/10.

